data commit_workflow_realization_bindings: List<CommitWorkflowRealizationBinding> = [
  CommitWorkflowRealizationBinding {
    surface: GithubActionsCiJob,
    handler: CiYamlHandler,
    artifact: CiYamlArtifact
  },
  CommitWorkflowRealizationBinding {
    surface: GitPrePushHook,
    handler: GitPrePushScriptHandler,
    artifact: GithooksPrePushArtifact
  }
]

fn commit_workflow_surface_eq(a: CommitWorkflowSurface, b: CommitWorkflowSurface) -> Bool {
  match a {
    GithubActionsCiJob =>
      match b { GithubActionsCiJob => true  _ => false }
    GithubActionsCiRegenJob =>
      match b { GithubActionsCiRegenJob => true  _ => false }
    GitPrePushHook =>
      match b { GitPrePushHook => true  _ => false }
    FalsifierCadenceJob =>
      match b { FalsifierCadenceJob => true  _ => false }
  }
}

fn surface_enrolled(surface: CommitWorkflowSurface, surfaces: List<CommitWorkflowSurface>) -> Bool {
  any(surfaces, s => commit_workflow_surface_eq(a: s, b: surface))
}

fn enrollment_has_surface(e: CommitCheckEnrollment, surface: CommitWorkflowSurface) -> Bool {
  surface_enrolled(surface: surface, surfaces: e.surfaces)
}

fn gate_eq(a: Gate, b: Gate) -> Bool {
  match a {
    EmitHostGate => match b { EmitHostGate => true  _ => false }
    CheapClaimPoolGate => match b { CheapClaimPoolGate => true  _ => false }
    ExtdepsExternalAuthorityGate => match b { ExtdepsExternalAuthorityGate => true  _ => false }
    DagCompileCleanGate => match b { DagCompileCleanGate => true  _ => false }
    GeneratedArtifactDriftGate => match b { GeneratedArtifactDriftGate => true  _ => false }
    SourceRootIngestGate => match b { SourceRootIngestGate => true  _ => false }
    RegenVerifyGate => match b { RegenVerifyGate => true  _ => false }
    SelfHostReadsRealBytesGate => match b { SelfHostReadsRealBytesGate => true  _ => false }
    SelfHostStalenessGate => match b { SelfHostStalenessGate => true  _ => false }
  }
}

fn gates_from_enrollments(rows: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<Gate> {
  fold(rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, row) {
    match row.check {
      CommitSpecGate { gate: g } => concat(acc, [g])
      CommitWitnessClaim { entry: _, check_fns: _, kind: _, span: _ } => acc
      CommitCargoFmtCheck => acc
    }
  })
}

fn project_ci_floor_gates(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<Gate> {
  gates_from_enrollments(
    rows: filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiJob))
  )
}

fn project_ci_regen_job_gates(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<Gate> {
  gates_from_enrollments(
    rows: filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiRegenJob))
  )
}

data gate_gauntlet_flip_basis_note: String = "THE MEASURED FLIPS (D3b, first application of the gate lane above). Basis is the per-run [gate-warm-cost] receipt the floor already emits — a real measurement at the grain the placement law requires for a GATE, which is why these three could be priced when the 36 CommitWitnessClaim rows still cannot: the TSV measures gates, and falsifier_cadence_surface_note's blocker is per-ROW receipts. Conflating the two grains would have been the fabrication that note forbids. Warm costs from the green composition run (30181042050, srv fleet arm64): source_root_ingest 427s as ONE opaque entry (its heartbeat reads 'entry 0 of 1' for ~8 minutes), self_host_realized_comparison 223s. Both are ORDERS above the 5s fast-lane budget (gunbc_ci_fast_lane_eval_budget_ms), so PrTier is inadmissible under ci_placement_law_note and Gauntlet is not a preference but the only admissible placement — no signature can make a 427s check fast-lane-eligible. THE COST, stated rather than elided: a regression in either now has up to a 4-hour detection window instead of one PR, and this is the same trade provenance_wall_cadence_rehome_risk accepted three days earlier, priced the same way. WHAT KEEPS IT FROM BEING A BARE NARROW is structural, not a promise: the gate lane's projector and batch land in the same change (falsifier_gate_projection_note), and gauntlet_lane_gate_rehome_is_never_bare_deenrollment_holds proves by execution that these rows reach an executing surface rather than vanishing. FOLLOW-ON TRIGGER, deliberately NOT taken here: a diff-proportional PR-tier proxy for source_root_ingest (ingest only the affected roots per-PR, full ingest on cadence) would return per-PR coverage at a cost that scales with the diff instead of the corpus — that is the real fix, and this flip is the interim that stops paying 427s per PR while it is built. THE THIRD GATE IS NOT FLIPPED, and the reason is a finding rather than caution: CheapClaimPoolGate (75s) is a declared member of v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan gunbc_ci_cheap_floor_gate_membership, which makes it BOTH a DataDependsOn predecessor of the compile root (floor_cheap_gates_precede_compile_edges) AND a floor_resource_anchor whose exclusion from corpus→gate serialization is what that list's own note says 'avoids a scheduler deadlock' (cheap→compile data order, corpus→cheap resource order, compile→corpus data order closing the cycle). Moving it is therefore a scheduler rewire, not a surface edit, for the smallest of the three prizes — 75s of the 725s measured. It stays per-PR pending an operator call on whether that rewire is worth 10 percent of the recovery. DECLINED 2026-07-26 (operator ruling): CheapClaimPoolGate gauntlet flip stays per-PR. REASON 1 — §6 displaced-cost bar: 75s is ~9% of the measured 725s warm cost, insufficient payoff for a scheduler rewire. REASON 2 — load-bearing signal + deadlock: as a DataDependsOn predecessor of the compile root it is the floor's earliest fail signal (moving it costs signal latency), and its exclusion from corpus→gate serialization avoids the three-way deadlock (cheap→compile data order, corpus→cheap resource order, compile→corpus data order). RE-OPEN TRIGGER: only when a lane restructures the floor scheduler for its own reasons (diff-proportional ingest proxy, or floor-memo M2) — never its own lane."

data falsifier_gate_projection_note: String = "The GATE half of the FalsifierCadenceJob lane, and it did not exist until 2026-07-26. FOUND BY AUDIT, not by a red: the lane shipped with a witness projector (project_falsifier_witness_entries) and no gate projector, while witness_entries_from_enrollments drops CommitSpecGate rows by construction (`CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => acc`). So a gate row moved to surfaces: [FalsifierCadenceJob] projected into NOTHING — it left the per-PR floor and arrived on no lane — and bare_deenrollment_wall_note's wall could not catch it because that wall filters on enrollment_is_witness_claim, which answers false for exactly this row kind. A gate was therefore the one enrollment shape that could be silently de-enrolled by a one-line surface edit that reads, in the diff, identically to a legitimate re-home. This projector plus gate_enrollment_is_scheduled close that: the lane can now receive gates, and the wall now counts them. THE ORDER MATTERS AND IS NOT COSMETIC: this projector and its executing batch (v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan gunbc_falsifier_gate_batch) land in the SAME change as the wall extension, because a wall that credits FalsifierCadenceJob for gates before any batch reads them would bless precisely the enrollment-by-illusion it exists to forbid — the same 'a surface tag with no batch reading it' trap falsifier_cadence_witness_batch_note names for witnesses."

fn project_falsifier_gates(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<Gate> {
  gates_from_enrollments(
    rows: filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: FalsifierCadenceJob))
  )
}

data ci_witness_optin_inversion: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "Opt-in inversion (operator, 2026-07-04) DISSOLVE FIRED at the discovery flip (operator acceptance 2026-07-09 on #6403; re-landed 2026-07-10, see gunbc.ci_spec ci_spec_discovery_flip_note): the corpus re-enrolled through CiSpec.discovery_scan_dirs with SelectionApplied, so per-PR CI runs tree-wide discovery shrunk to the diff's affected set. The scaffold's dissolve-on (affected-set selection + floor memoization make per-PR selection-by-affectedness affordable) is satisfied at discovery width=1 under union-resolve S1. project_ci_floor_witness_entries is Terminal, not interim: CommitWitnessClaim rows remain live as the explicit-entry roster (execution-kind rows with their own resource profile, and any row that must run as declared) - only the roster's EXCLUSIVITY as witness source dissolved."
}

data witness_projection_explicit_arms_note: String = "The enrollment projections match EXPLICITLY on every CommitCheckKind variant (no wildcard arm): a future variant added to the coproduct then reds every projection at compile time instead of being silently dropped by a `_ => acc` absorption - fail-open enrollment (a declared row contributing zero entries with no diagnostic) is unwritable, not detected."

fn witness_entries_from_enrollments(rows: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  fold(rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, row) {
    match row.check {
      CommitWitnessClaim { entry, check_fns, kind, span: _ } =>
        if check_fns.count() == 0 {
          concat(acc, [ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: "", kind: kind }])
        } else {
          concat(acc, fold(check_fns, init: [], f: fn(fns, check_fn) {
            concat(fns, [ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: check_fn, kind: kind }])
          }))
        }
      CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => acc
      CommitCargoFmtCheck => acc
    }
  })
}

fn project_ci_floor_witness_entries(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  witness_entries_from_enrollments(
    rows: filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiJob))
  )
}

data falsifier_cadence_surface_note: String = "FalsifierCadenceJob is the SCHEDULED home for declared witness rows whose measured wall prices them out of the per-PR floor (batch-4 clamp FLOOR-BATCH-OVER-BUDGET, run 30148859947: wall_ms=613864 vs clamp_ms=420000 at units=74; authority gunbc.ci_spec gunbc_ci_floor_batch_clamp_params[3]). It extends the axis that ALREADY answers 'where does this check run' — the enrollment surface — rather than minting a second re-home authority beside gunbc.ci_layer_roots falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_rows, which is specifically the bin_witness_wet_entries per-row-budget overflow (its constructor is bin_wet, its budget datum is bin_witness_wet_per_row_wall_budget_seconds) and does not model CommitWitnessClaim rows. Re-homing here is NEVER a bare de-enrollment: a row moved off GithubActionsCiJob must land on this surface, so it stays enrolled somewhere and its execution is receipted on the 4-hour cadence. The failure mode this guards is measured, not hypothetical — 63 *_test.dag files live under the two test/claim/long/ dirs, 9 are enrolled here, and the rest are enrolled NOWHERE (long/ is excluded from discovery at dir grain and the falsifier does not walk it), so 'deferred' has historically meant 'unscheduled'; this surface is the lane those rows enroll into. GRAIN: enrollment splits at the check_fn, not the file — an entry whose expensive fns re-home keeps its cheap fns on GithubActionsCiJob as the per-PR smoke grain (the mocks-layer-never-replace rule), so a re-home costs the corpus its wet grain per-PR, never the concern's per-PR coverage entirely. 🟡 dissolve-on: v2.workflow.ci_placement Placement (PrTier | Gauntlet) supersedes this surface tag as the witness-scheduling authority. It cannot today: PrTier is unwritable without a WarmCostReceipt { measured_ms, run_ref } AND measured_ms <= gunbc_ci_fast_lane_eval_budget_ms (5s), so wiring placement onto the 36 CommitWitnessClaim rows requires a per-row measured receipt for each — the D2 warm-cost probe on fleet srv hardware is the named filler (ci_placement_law_note), and it has not run. Fabricating those receipts would be the fail-open the placement law exists to forbid; defaulting the unmeasured rows to Gauntlet would de-enroll all 36 at once. Encouraging convergence receipt: the 5s law selects EXACTLY the twelve rows the run-30148859947 slow-witness tables measured over 5s (group A 141s/57s/15s/7s, group B 141s/29s/27s/14s/13s/13s/13s/13s) and admits every other batch-4 row at <=1s, so placement and this surface agree on today's roster — the wiring is blocked on receipts, not on a disputed boundary."

data provenance_wall_cadence_rehome_risk: String = "ACCEPTED RISK, recorded where it was decided (operator ruling 2026-07-25). Three affected-set provenance walls — lens_affected_set_provenance_producer_rejects_malformed_ingest_holds, _rejects_beyond_surface_ingest_holds, _coverage_receipt_holds (14s + 13s + 13s measured, run 30148859947 group-B slow-witness table) — move from per-PR to the 4-hour falsifier cadence. THE COST: a selection-provenance regression now has up to a 24-hour detection window instead of one PR. THE CONTEXT THAT MAKES THIS UNCOMFORTABLE, stated rather than elided: this is accepted in the same week that exact class let #7196's stale slice control ride main green — the infer_semantics witness's transport (dag/tools/infer_semantics_witness_transport.dag) declares no dependency on v1_compiler_infer_access.rs, so the affected set could not see the edge and main's run at bb4347d skipped 1761 of 2373 witnesses, that one among them (fixed as a control by #7222; the SELECTION escape is untouched). WHAT KEEPS THIS FROM BEING A BARE NARROW: the four cheap fns of the same file stay per-PR (single_read_emits_row, parse_coverage_known_diff_fail_closed, git_diff_wire, unknown_diff_fail_closed — all <=161ms), so the producer keeps per-PR coverage at the fixture grain and loses only the wet grain; and gauntlet_lane_enrollment_witness_test proves by execution that these rows are cadence-enrolled rather than merely dropped. 🟡 dissolve-on — THE COMPENSATING CONTROL, which converts this from cadence-detection to construction: v2.lens.affected_set.declared_source_ref_selection today answers NoDeclaredSourceRefs => false in declared_source_refs_blocks_skip, i.e. a witness that declares NO source refs does not block its own skip — the precise fail-open #7196 rode. When the SourceRef child lands declared source-ref edges on witness transports AND that arm flips to refuse (NoDeclaredSourceRefs => true, an undeclared-provenance witness is never skippable), the wall is CONSTRUCTION rather than a witness watching for the breach, and these three rows can stay cadence-only permanently. Until that flip, this row is the standing record that per-PR detection was traded away deliberately, priced at 40s of a 194s clamp breach."

fn project_falsifier_witness_entries(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  witness_entries_from_enrollments(
    rows: filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: FalsifierCadenceJob))
  )
}

fn enrollment_is_witness_claim(e: CommitCheckEnrollment) -> Bool {
  match e.check {
    CommitWitnessClaim { entry: _, check_fns: _, kind: _, span: _ } => true
    CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => false
    CommitCargoFmtCheck => false
  }
}

fn witness_enrollment_is_scheduled(e: CommitCheckEnrollment) -> Bool {
  enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiJob)
    || enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: FalsifierCadenceJob)
}

fn enrollment_is_spec_gate(e: CommitCheckEnrollment) -> Bool {
  match e.check {
    CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => true
    CommitWitnessClaim { entry: _, check_fns: _, kind: _, span: _ } => false
    CommitCargoFmtCheck => false
  }
}

data gate_enrollment_surface_asymmetry_note: String = "WHY GATES NEED THEIR OWN SCHEDULED-SURFACE PREDICATE rather than reusing witness_enrollment_is_scheduled: the two row kinds disagree about ONE surface, and the disagreement is a fact about which projector executes which kind, not a policy preference. GithubActionsCiRegenJob EXECUTES gates — project_ci_regen_job_gates reads it, and RegenVerifyGate/SelfHostStalenessGate ride it as their only surface — so for a gate it is a genuine enforcement authority. For a WITNESS it is not, and bare_deenrollment_wall_note says exactly why: 'the regen job projects GATES only', so a witness parked there executes nowhere. Folding both kinds into one predicate would therefore have to either wrongly credit witnesses on the regen job (re-opening the hole that note closed) or wrongly deny gates their real home (redding RegenVerifyGate, a correctly-enrolled row). GitPrePushHook counts for NEITHER, for the reason the standing ruling already gives: opt-in per clone, bypassable with --no-verify, absent in container worktrees, and PROVEN ineffective by #6658. So the shared law is 'a declared row must ride a surface that executes ITS kind', and the two predicates are that one law read against two projector sets — not two policies."

fn gate_enrollment_is_scheduled(e: CommitCheckEnrollment) -> Bool {
  enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiJob)
    || enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GithubActionsCiRegenJob)
    || enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: FalsifierCadenceJob)
}

fn bare_deenrolled_gate_rows(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<CommitCheckEnrollment> {
  filter(roster, e => enrollment_is_spec_gate(e: e) && !gate_enrollment_is_scheduled(e: e))
}

fn roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_gate(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> Bool {
  bare_deenrolled_gate_rows(roster: roster).count() == 0
}

fn live_roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_gate() -> Bool {
  roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_gate(roster: commit_gate_roster)
}

fn live_roster_falsifier_gates() -> List<Gate> {
  project_falsifier_gates(roster: commit_gate_roster)
}

data doc_reachability_cadence_enrollment_note: String = "FOUND BY THE WALL, on its first execution (2026-07-25). gauntlet_lane_rehome_is_never_bare_deenrollment_holds redded against the LIVE roster, not a synthetic fixture: the doc-reachability witness (doc_graph_has_no_orphan_docs, doc_graph_has_no_dangling_links) rode surfaces: [GitPrePushHook] alone — enforced only by a mechanism this repo has already ruled is NOT an enforcement authority (commit_gate_rust_suite_removed_disposition: opt-in per clone via core.hooksPath, bypassable with --no-verify, absent in container worktrees, and PROVEN ineffective — #6658 landed an unformatted .rs on main 2026-07-15 and nothing caught it). So orphaned docs and dangling doc links have had no wall on any CI path; they were one --no-verify from landing. FIXED by adding FalsifierCadenceJob rather than by widening witness_enrollment_is_scheduled to accept GitPrePushHook — widening the predicate until the failure disappears is the absorbing fallback §5 forbids, and it would have re-buried the finding in the same motion that surfaced it. The hook enrollment STAYS for fast local feedback; the cadence row is the authority. Kind is CorpusWitnessKind, not ExecutionWitnessKind: it reads the live doc graph, so per-PR admission would need a warm-cost receipt this change does not have — the same D2-probe gap falsifier_cadence_surface_note records. Promoting it to per-PR when that receipt exists is a strict improvement, not a requirement of this change."

data bare_deenrollment_wall_note: String = "The construction wall behind falsifier_cadence_surface_note's 'a re-home is NEVER a bare de-enrollment'. A CommitWitnessClaim row must ride at least one EXECUTING witness surface — GithubActionsCiJob (per-PR floor) or FalsifierCadenceJob (4-hour cadence). GithubActionsCiRegenJob and GitPrePushHook do not count: the regen job projects GATES only (project_ci_regen_job_gates), and the pre-push hook is an escape hatch by the standing ruling (opt-in per clone, bypassable with --no-verify, absent in container worktrees — commit_gate_rust_suite_removed_disposition), so neither is an enforcement authority for a witness. A row satisfying neither is enrolled NOWHERE while still LOOKING enrolled, which is precisely the ~54-dark-file state test/claim/long/ is in and the shape a lazy re-home would add to. This is detection, not construction (the surface list is still writable as []) — the honest classification per DESIGN §5: it reds in the per-PR floor via gauntlet_lane_enrollment_witness_test with a synthetic RED control, and the construction form waits on the same D2-probe-gated placement wiring as falsifier_cadence_surface_note's dissolve-on, where Gauntlet-vs-PrTier is total over the coproduct and 'neither' becomes unwritable rather than merely counted. AMENDED 2026-07-26: this note described the witness half only, and that scoping was itself the gap — CommitSpecGate rows had NO such wall, so the one row kind whose de-enrollment nothing could catch was the one the Gauntlet lane was about to be used on. The gate half is now gate_enrollment_is_scheduled / roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_gate, with the surface asymmetry (regen counts for gates, never for witnesses) reasoned in gate_enrollment_surface_asymmetry_note. Both halves are still DETECTION, not construction, and both dissolve on the same placement wiring."

fn bare_deenrolled_witness_rows(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<CommitCheckEnrollment> {
  filter(roster, e => enrollment_is_witness_claim(e: e) && !witness_enrollment_is_scheduled(e: e))
}

fn roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_witness(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> Bool {
  bare_deenrolled_witness_rows(roster: roster).count() == 0
}

fn live_roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_witness() -> Bool {
  roster_has_no_bare_deenrolled_witness(roster: commit_gate_roster)
}

fn live_roster_falsifier_witness_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  project_falsifier_witness_entries(roster: commit_gate_roster)
}

fn witness_seam_eq(a: WitnessSeam, b: WitnessSeam) -> Bool {
  (a.producer == b.producer) && (a.consumer == b.consumer)
}

fn witness_seam_wellformed(seam: WitnessSeam) -> Bool {
  !(seam.producer == seam.consumer)
}

fn seam_list_contains(seams: List<WitnessSeam>, seam: WitnessSeam) -> Bool {
  fold(seams, init: false, f: fn(acc, s) { acc || witness_seam_eq(a: s, b: seam) })
}

fn seams_wellformed_and_distinct(seams: List<WitnessSeam>) -> Bool {
  if seams.count() == 0 {
    true
  } else {
    witness_seam_wellformed(seam: seams.first())
      && !seam_list_contains(seams: seams.skip(n: 1), seam: seams.first())
      && seams_wellformed_and_distinct(seams: seams.skip(n: 1))
  }
}

fn witness_span_wellformed(span: WitnessSpan) -> Bool {
  match span {
    SpanUndeclared => true
    SpanSeams { seams } => seams.count() > 0 && seams_wellformed_and_distinct(seams: seams)
  }
}

fn roster_witness_spans_wellformed(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> Bool {
  fold(roster, init: true, f: fn(acc, row) {
    match row.check {
      CommitWitnessClaim { entry: _, check_fns: _, kind: _, span } =>
        acc && witness_span_wellformed(span: span)
      CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => acc
      CommitCargoFmtCheck => acc
    }
  })
}

fn local_tidy_check_eq(a: LocalTidyCheck, b: LocalTidyCheck) -> Bool {
  match a {
    LocalTidyWitnessCheck { entry, check_fns } =>
      match b {
        LocalTidyWitnessCheck { entry: entry2, check_fns: check_fns2 } =>
          entry == entry2 && string_list_eq(left: check_fns, right: check_fns2)
        _ => false
      }
    LocalTidyCargoFmtCheck =>
      match b { LocalTidyCargoFmtCheck => true  _ => false }
  }
}

fn project_local_tidy_checks(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<LocalTidyCheck> {
  let pre_push = filter(roster, e => enrollment_has_surface(e: e, surface: GitPrePushHook))
  concat(
    project_local_tidy_witness_rows(roster: pre_push),
    project_local_tidy_fmt_rows(roster: pre_push)
  )
}

fn project_local_tidy_witness_rows(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<LocalTidyCheck> {
  fold(roster, init: [], f: fn(acc, row) {
    match row.check {
      CommitWitnessClaim { entry, check_fns, kind: _, span: _ } =>
        concat(acc, [LocalTidyWitnessCheck { entry: entry, check_fns: check_fns }])
      CommitSpecGate { gate: _ } => acc
      CommitCargoFmtCheck => acc
    }
  })
}

fn project_local_tidy_fmt_rows(roster: List<CommitCheckEnrollment>) -> List<LocalTidyCheck> {
  fold(roster, init: [], f: fn(acc, row) {
    match row.check {
      CommitCargoFmtCheck => concat(acc, [LocalTidyCargoFmtCheck])
      _ => acc
    }
  })
}

fn gate_lists_eq(left: List<Gate>, right: List<Gate>) -> Bool {
  if length(left) != length(right) {
    false
  } else if length(left) == 0 {
    true
  } else if !gate_eq(a: left.first(), b: right.first()) {
    false
  } else {
    gate_lists_eq(left: left.skip(n: 1), right: right.skip(n: 1))
  }
}

fn local_tidy_lists_eq(left: List<LocalTidyCheck>, right: List<LocalTidyCheck>) -> Bool {
  if length(left) != length(right) {
    false
  } else if length(left) == 0 {
    true
  } else if !local_tidy_check_eq(a: left.first(), b: right.first()) {
    false
  } else {
    local_tidy_lists_eq(left: left.skip(n: 1), right: right.skip(n: 1))
  }
}

data commit_workflow_ci_floor_gates: List<Gate> = project_ci_floor_gates(roster: commit_gate_roster)

data commit_workflow_local_tidy_checks: List<LocalTidyCheck> = project_local_tidy_checks(roster: commit_gate_roster)

fn ci_floor_commit_witness_claim_schedule() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  project_ci_floor_witness_entries(roster: commit_gate_roster)
}

fn realization_artifact_path(surface: CommitWorkflowSurface) -> String {
  match surface {
    GithubActionsCiJob => artifact_path(a: CiYamlArtifact)
    GithubActionsCiRegenJob => artifact_path(a: CiYamlArtifact)
    GitPrePushHook => artifact_path(a: GithooksPrePushArtifact)
    FalsifierCadenceJob => artifact_path(a: FalsifierYamlArtifact)
  }
}

fn realization_handler_for_surface(surface: CommitWorkflowSurface) -> CommitWorkflowRealizationKind {
  match surface {
    GithubActionsCiJob => CiYamlHandler
    GithubActionsCiRegenJob => CiYamlHandler
    GitPrePushHook => GitPrePushScriptHandler
    FalsifierCadenceJob => CiYamlHandler
  }
}

fn realization_artifact_for_surface(surface: CommitWorkflowSurface) -> GeneratedArtifact {
  match surface {
    GithubActionsCiJob => CiYamlArtifact
    GithubActionsCiRegenJob => CiYamlArtifact
    GitPrePushHook => GithooksPrePushArtifact
    FalsifierCadenceJob => FalsifierYamlArtifact
  }
}

data commit_workflow_long_lane_note: String = "Two complexity-lens enrollments (fold_lowering_test, accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test) DELETED from the GithubActionsCiJob surface 2026-07-12: their check_fns measured over the fast-lane 5-second witness eval budget (operator rule; authority gunbc_ci_fast_lane_rule_note in v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan), and an explicit enrollment row bypasses discovery exclusion, so re-pathing the row to test/claim/long/ would keep the over-budget rows on every PR. Offlining an explicit row means deleting its declaration, never teaching exclusions to veto the roster (the enforcement-coverage precedent in gunbc.ci_layer_roots). The files live under src/v2/test/claim/long/ with the local recipe; dissolve-on: the long-lane scheduled trigger (falsifier follow-on) enrolls them and this note retires. Contrast: the parse_table_memo_governed enrollment above was REPOINTED to its long/ home, not deleted — its four enrolled check_fns each measured 0ms (audit 2026-07-12); only unenrolled siblings in that file (warm_equals_cold) are over budget, and an explicit row runs exactly its named check_fns. Delete when the enrolled fns themselves are slow; repoint when only the file moved. Wave 1 Gate 1 body-producer keystones (wave1_gate1_b1_bare_call_body_producer_witness_test.dag, wave1_gate1_a1_symbol_index_body_producer_witness_test.dag — five enrolled check_fns, ~5s+ each under floor load) were DELETED 2026-07-14 for the same reason: explicit rows bypass test/claim/long/ discovery exclusion, so affected-set selection on PRs touching target_model.dag (live case #6589) enrolled them into the 5s fast lane and REDed at EvalBudgetExceeded (~5013ms). Fast receipts stay in self_host/ (discovered); execution proofs stay in long/ (local recipe: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <file> --functions <csv>). Separately, two rows (parse_test floor/perf, dag_compile_clean_perturb_receipts) were DELETED 2026-07-12 as §3 de-duplication, not offlining: the same check_fns are declared in gunbc.ci_layer_roots bin_witness_wet_entries (the Wet bin-execution lane), and the double enrollment ran them a second time inside the HERMETIC corpus batch, where their run_witness_bin host effects refuse (CI receipt: run 29208529942, IsExecutable refusals). One fact, one roster: the bin lane keeps the per-PR coverage."

data wave1_gate1_d_census_class_c_split_note: String = "wave1_gate1_d_census (test-decomposition-wcf-cut.md Class C row, ~141s measured) split 2026-07-25: attribution-by-execution (claim_batch, cold) showed the census's ENROLLED per-PR check_fn ran a witness wall of 134526ms against a one-time 32034ms entry-closure resolve — the cost lives in the witness body itself, which builds 10 ingested_fixture_arrows fixtures (each a real tokenize->parse_module->normalize->resolve pass) across two aggregator fns; this is genuine corpus breadth (Class C), not a fixture-shaped cost-shape defect (Class F ruled out by measurement, not by assumption). The mechanism-only sibling (self_host/wave1_gate1_d_mvp_subsumption_witness_test.dag's five table_fixture check_fns, measured eval_self=0.000ms each on a cold run — proves Arrow+body well-formedness/behavior-kind mechanism via table_fixture producers, no census ingest) carries no explicit CommitCheckEnrollment here: it is already picked up per-PR by the source-root *_test.dag discovery walk (ci_spec_discovery_flip_note), so an explicit roster row would be a second, redundant admission path for the same DiscoverySelection-covered file — a §3 duplication, not an accept requirement (a check_fn that is unconditionally discovered needs no roster entry to run). The real census-ingest execution (wave1_gate1_d_census_subsumption_witness_holds, long/wave1_gate1_d_mvp_subsumption_witness_test.dag) is re-homed off per-PR discovery onto the falsifier's 4-hourly cadence as one more row on falsifier_substrate_long_lane_entries (v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan gunbc_falsifier_substrate_long_lane_batch; frontier row in gunbc.ci_layer_roots falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows, joining the sibling provenance-producer rows from PR #7230/test-decomposition-wcf-cut.md) — the single hermetic long-lane falsifier consumer for this witness class, not a parallel batch: this witness is ExecutionWitnessKind/SubstrateInputsOnly interpreted computation with no host effects, so folding it into the subprocess-execution Wet lane (falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_batch) would be a §3 nickname. A WitnessExclusionRow (pattern \"long/wave1_gate1_d_mvp_subsumption_witness_test.dag\", classification FalsifierSubstrateLongLane) carves the file out of per-PR discovery so the classification is honest, not a lie against an unhandled default. Enrolled, but NOT unconditionally executed — the original claim here ('the row always executes on the 4-hourly cadence') was falsified by the lane's first scheduled run (30176416535, 2026-07-25) and is corrected 2026-07-26: batch 6 declares node_frontier_selection: SelectionApplied and the falsifier diffs GUNBC_CI_DIFF_BASE=HEAD~20, so affected-set selection — a per-PR mechanism, like the fast-lane eval budget that mis-scoped onto the same lane — also applies here. That run reported '10 witness(es) across 3 entr(y/ies) · 1 unaffected (import-closure, skipped without resolve) · 9 in the affected closure' and emitted result lines for only 7: this census row and the two edit_locus rows produced NO receipt and were counted as not-failed. So the honest statement is that enrollment is non-empty and the row executes on the cadences where the last 20 commits touch its closure; a silent skip is indistinguishable from a pass in the batch tally today. Whether this lane should run SelectionOff (unconditional coverage, ~127-135s per cadence for this row alone) is an open cost/cadence decision, not settled here. Dissolve-on: the census ingest's per-fixture pipeline cost drops under the per-PR fast-lane budget on a measured cold run (e.g. shared parse-table/resolve memoization landing for this closure) — then re-enroll wave1_gate1_d_census_subsumption_witness_holds per-PR discovery and delete the falsifier_substrate_long_lane_rows entry, the exclusion row, and this note."
